igh-thrust-high-v_e concept \u2014 nuclear thermal, nuclear electric, fusion, Orion \u2014 is nuclear. It is not a coincidence but a theorem, and F = 2P/v_e is its proof: the constraint is thermodynamic, not technological."}, {"id": "q7", "type": "open", "prompt": "There are exactly two ways to break the chemical exhaust-velocity wall, suited to opposite jobs, and the chapter offers a single skill for judging any propulsion proposal. Lay out the two routes, why each suits its job, and the skill \u2014 and connect it to the unit's through-line.", "rubric": "Two routes, because there are exactly two ways to break the wall. (1) Change HOW you accelerate the exhaust: electric fields instead of heat \u2014 ion propulsion, v_e \u2248 30 km/s (ten times the wall), by ionizing atoms and accelerating them electrically (voltage sets the speed, with no thermal or molecular-weight ceiling). It chooses high v_e and feeble thrust, so it is useless for leaving a gravity well but supreme for the patient, propellant-starved work of deep space \u2014 which is why it has taken over deep-space science, geostationary station-keeping, and megaconstellations. (2) Change the WORKING FLUID and heat source: heat pure hydrogen (M = 2) with a fission reactor instead of combustion \u2014 nuclear thermal, v_e \u2248 9 km/s (double the wall) at high thrust, because the reactor's gigawatt power keeps F = 2P/v_e from biting. It suits crewed missions that need both reasonable transit time and a sane mass ratio. The skill: judge every proposal with two tools \u2014 the rocket equation (does the \u0394v close if v_e is high enough?) and F = 2P/v_e (does the power source permit the claimed thrust AND v_e?). Ask of any engine: what is the power source, and does the trade allow what they claim? That sorts real from fantastical \u2014 why ion drives are feeble (weak power), why antimatter is forbidden by the stockroom not the physics, why Orion was killed by a treaty not a theorem, and why the high-performance future is unavoidably nuclear. The through-line \u2014 never carry anything through a \u0394v it does not need to experience \u2014 reaches its purest expression here: ion propulsion carries almost no propellant at all (mass ratio near 1), defeating the exponential not by dropping mass along the way, as staging does, but by needing so little mass to begin with. High exhaust velocity is the ultimate way to carry less."}]$l6_quiz$::jsonb as questions
